# citation.cff for the effectbridge package
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "effectbridge: Test Unconfoundedness by Comparing RCT and Observational Effects"
abstract: >
  R package to test (un)confoundedness by comparing a marginal treatment effect
  estimated in an RCT-like dataset with the same estimand from an observational
  dataset. Supports IPW, AIPW (doubly robust), TMLE, G-computation, and matching
  estimators, multiple effect measures (RD, RR, OR), bootstrap and analytical
  inference, optional transportability weighting (manual or auto-detected via
  KS/energy tests), comprehensive diagnostics, and sensitivity analysis.
authors:
  - family-names: Ribeiro
    given-names: Diogo
    email: diogo.debastos.ribeiro@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-2022-7072"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2025-08-29"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DiogoRibeiro7/effectbridge"
url: "https://diogoribeiro7.github.io/packages/effectbridge/"
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - unconfoundedness
  - inverse probability weighting
  - augmented IPW
  - doubly robust
  - transportability
  - density ratio
  - bootstrap
  - R

